    // ----- goto and labels -----
    // A labelled statement is pushed as {lbl, t} instead of a bare thunk, so the
    // enclosing statement SEQUENCE can index its labels. A goto returns a signal that
    // every enclosing construct passes upward (exactly like a return) until a sequence
    // that knows the label catches it and resumes there - which covers forward jumps,
    // backward jumps and jumps out of nested loops alike.
